🚽 Test case: #196 -- a pointer-to-struct/union FUNCTION PARAMETER
🚽 (`skibidi f(gang Point *pp)`) can do `pp.field` the same as a
🚽 pointer-typed local variable, and a write through it is visible to
🚽 the caller (real aliasing, not a copy). Before PR #248 review finding
🚽 3's fix, enter_function_scope() never copied the parameter's
🚽 struct_name onto the bound runtime Variable, so this died on "Unknown
🚽 struct or union type" even though the analyzer already accepted it.
gang Point {
    rizz x;
    rizz y;
};

skibidi bump(gang Point *pp) {
    pp.x = 99;
}

skibidi main {
    gang Point p;
    p.x = 5;
    bump(&p);
    yapping("%d", p.x);
}
